# @@name@@

A production-minded service built with [zapline](https://github.com/samsamurai301/zapline):
typed routes, validation, OpenAPI docs, layered configuration, dependency
injection, health probes, Prometheus metrics, tracing and a hardened middleware
stack.

```sh
zapline dev          # rebuild and restart on every change
cargo run            # or run once
cargo test           # in-process tests, no sockets
```

| URL | What |
|---|---|
| <http://localhost:8080/docs> | Swagger UI |
| <http://localhost:8080/openapi.json> | OpenAPI 3.1 document |
| <http://localhost:8080/health/live> | Liveness probe |
| <http://localhost:8080/health/ready> | Readiness probe (runs the registered checks) |
| <http://localhost:8080/metrics> | Prometheus metrics |
| <http://localhost:8080/_dev> | Dev console: routes and recent requests (debug builds only) |

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs` | `app(&settings)`: wires dependencies, probes, metrics, middleware, routes |
| `src/main.rs` | Loads settings, starts tracing, serves the app |
| `src/config.rs` | Typed `Settings` |
| `config/*.toml` | Layered configuration files |
| `src/repository.rs` | `UserRepository` trait and an in-memory implementation |
| `src/models.rs` | Request and response types with validation rules |
| `src/routes/` | One module per resource; each exposes `mount(app)` |
| `tests/` | Integration tests using `app(&settings).test()` |

## Configuration

Settings are layered, lowest priority first:

1. `config/default.toml`
2. `config/{APP_ENV}.toml`: `APP_ENV` defaults to `development`; the Docker image uses `production`
3. environment variables named `APP__SECTION__KEY`, for example `APP__SERVER__PORT=9000`

Add a field to `Settings` in `src/config.rs` and a default in
`config/default.toml`, and it is available everywhere. Never commit secrets:
supply them through the environment.

## Dependency injection

`src/lib.rs` registers the repository once:

```rust
.provide_dyn::<dyn UserRepository>(Arc::new(MemUserRepository::default()))
```

Handlers ask for it with `repo: Dep<dyn UserRepository>`. Implement the trait
for your database and change that one line.

## Middleware stack

Request IDs, tracing, security headers, CORS, per-IP rate limiting (100
requests/minute), response compression and panic catching are installed in
`src/lib.rs`. `Cors::permissive()` is a development default: restrict the
allowed origins before you deploy.

## Adding endpoints

```sh
zapline generate resource post      # src/routes/posts.rs + tests/posts.rs, mounted for you
zapline generate handler ping       # a single route
zapline routes                      # print the route table
zapline openapi -o openapi.json     # export the OpenAPI document
```

## Docker

```sh
docker build -t @@name@@ .
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 @@name@@
```

A multi-stage build compiles the binary, then a slim Debian image runs it as a
non-root user with `APP_ENV=production`. Point your orchestrator's probes at
`/health/live` and `/health/ready`, and Prometheus at `/metrics`.

## CI

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`
and `cargo test` on every push and pull request.
